System clipboard bridges for the remote context: programs on the server reaching
the real clipboard of the machine the browser runs on.

- OSC 52: the browser clipboard service mirrors regular 'clipboard'-type
  writes to the system clipboard best-effort, so terminal programs copying via
  OSC 52 reach it. The write can reject when the tab is unfocused or the
  browser demands a user gesture it never had (an OSC 52 write arrives from
  the pty stream, not a tap) - the in-memory copy stays as the fallback and we
  never steal focus to force it.
- CLI: --clipboard-out / --clipboard-image-out / --clipboard-image-in pipe
  text and PNG images over the remote CLI channel, with writeImage threaded
  through the clipboard services end to end. The rootfs wl-copy / xclip / xsel
  shims sit on top of these flags.

